>> title: Harissa
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: tunisian, chiles, paste, caraway, condiment
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: harissa paste, hot sauce, the red one
>> pairs-with: toum, harira
>> servings: 12
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: narrow — the caraway and coriander get two minutes and no more; a paste built on scorched seed is bitter for the month it keeps

>> step: soak 20 min, drain
Soak @dried guajillo chiles{4}(stemmed and seeded) and @dried chiles de arbol{6}(stemmed) in @boiling water{2%cups}(480 mL) for ~{20%min}, then drain them.

>> step: toast 2 min, grind
Toast @caraway seeds{2%tsp}, @coriander seeds{2%tsp}, and @cumin seeds{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat for ~{2%min}, then grind them in a #spice grinder{}.

>> step: blend to a thick paste
Blend @&(~2)drained chiles{} with @&(~1)ground spices{}, @garlic{4%cloves}, and @kosher salt{2%tsp} to a thick paste in a #food processor{}.

>> step: blend in
Blend @extra-virgin olive oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL) and @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into @&(~1)harissa{}.
